; Five, one per condition — and five rather than six is itself the
; assertion. A self-reference is technically also a cycle, but it has its own
; more specific diagnostic, so the cycle walk skips self-edges rather than
; saying the same thing twice in different words.
;
; The path is `[<form>, <key>, requires]`, naming the declaration that is
; wrong rather than the form as a whole.
(diagnostics
  (diagnostic :code invalid_manifest :path [self a requires])
  (diagnostic :code invalid_manifest :path [unknown a requires])
  (diagnostic :code invalid_manifest :path [always a requires])
  (diagnostic :code invalid_manifest :path [grouped a requires])
  (diagnostic :code invalid_manifest :path [cycle y requires]))
